1920. Build Array from Permutation

Description:
Given a permutation array nums, create a new array ans where:

ans[i] = nums[nums[i]]

Return the new array ans.

Test Case:

Input:  nums = [0,2,1,5,3,4]
Output: [0,1,2,4,5,3]

Why?

ans[0] = nums[nums[0]] = nums[0] = 0
ans[1] = nums[nums[1]] = nums[2] = 1
ans[2] = nums[nums[2]] = nums[1] = 2

Following the same process gives [0,1,2,4,5,3].
class Solution {
    public int[] buildArray(int[] nums) {
        int n=nums.length;
        int[] arr = new int[n];
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            int num = nums[nums[i]];
            arr[i] = num;
        }
        return arr;
    }
}
